#: ../../source/components_basic/02-component_gas.rst:18
msgid "Gas/Smoke Sensor Module (MQ2)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/components_basic/02-component_gas.rst:25
msgid "Introduction"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/components_basic/02-component_gas.rst:26
msgid "The MQ-2 sensor is a versatile gas sensor capable of detecting a wide range of gases including alcohol, carbon monoxide, hydrogen, isobutene, liquefied petroleum gas, methane, propane, and smoke. It is popular among beginners due to its low cost and easy-to-use features."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/components_basic/02-component_gas.rst:29
msgid "Principle"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/components_basic/02-component_gas.rst:30
msgid "The MQ-2 sensor works on the principle of resistance changes in the presence of different gases. When the target gas comes in contact with the heated MOS(Metal Oxide Semiconductor) material, it undergoes oxidation or reduction reactions that change the resistance of the MOS material. **It is noteworthy that the MQ2 gas sensor is capable of detecting multiple gases, but lacks the ability to differentiate between them.** This is a common characteristic of most gas sensors."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/components_basic/02-component_gas.rst:32
msgid "The sensor has a built-in potentiometer that allows you to adjust the sensor digital output (D0) threshold. When the concentration of gas in the air exceeds a certain threshold value, the resistance of the sensor changes. This change in resistance is then converted into an electrical signal that can be read by an Arduino board."
msgstr ""

