msgstr ""

#: ../../source/components_basic/02-component_gas.rst:71
msgid "The first line of code is a constant integer declaration for the gas sensor pin. We use the analog pin A0 to read the output from the gas sensor."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/components_basic/02-component_gas.rst:77
msgid "The ``setup()`` function is where we initialize our serial communication at a baud rate of 9600. This is necessary to print the readings from the gas sensor to the serial monitor."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/components_basic/02-component_gas.rst:85
msgid "The ``loop()`` function is where we continuously read the analog value from the gas sensor and print it to the serial monitor. We use the ``analogRead()`` function to read the analog value from the sensor. We then wait for 50 milliseconds before the next reading. This delay gives some breathing space for the serial monitor to process the data."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/components_basic/02-component_gas.rst:97
msgid "MQ2 is a heating-driven sensor that usually requires preheating before use. During the preheating period, the sensor typically reads high and gradually decreases until it stabilizes."
msgstr ""

